arning Resource Services. This is a temporary full-time position located on-site in Athabasca, with an end date of August 2027. The Position: The Manager, Learning Resource Services manages internal processes related to Course Materials, Acquisition, Inventory, Warehouse Control and Shipping, and Student Services. They provide management of Learning Resource Services to ensure efficient and effective unit operation, including budget management and external liaison. Qualifications: A four-year University degree, preferably in business. May consider an equivalent combination of education and experience, where that experience includes at least 9 years directly relevant work experience in a learning resources setting with budget and managerial experience. A minimum of 5 years related work and supervisory experience in a unionized environment, some of which should be at a post-secondary institution. The incumbent should have excellent interpersonal skills and experience in resource allocation, organizational planning, and management of computerized systems and technology. Systems utilized include CMIS, Banner, and a variety of reporting tools. Demonstrated success in the implementation of major projects is required. Demonstrated interpersonal skills, including facilitation and negotiation skills is required. Must possess strong conceptual, analytical and creative problem-solving abilities. Excellent computer program and systems skills required. Experience leading and managing collaborative client relationships and teams is preferred. Professional experience within a post-secondary setting is preferred. Supervisory skills, A detailed job description can be viewed at: Manager, Learning Resource Services. Contact Information: For more information regarding this role, please contact Elaine Fabbro, Interim AVP Learner Experience, at elainef@athabascau.ca . Work at AU A university like no other for people like no other Athabasca University (AU) has widened access and increased